From: Gleb Pesin <dormancygrace@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 00:11:33 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] vpu: a blocking state wait sleeps instead of spinning

In block mode cviVPU_LockAndCheck took the codec lock, found the
instance in another state, released the lock and called cond_resched in
a loop: it spun on the CPU, and took and released the lock (sleeping
and waking the core) on every turn. It now sleeps 200-400 us
between checks.
---
 interdrv/cvi_vc_drv/vcodec/vpuapi/vpuapi.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/interdrv/cvi_vc_drv/vcodec/vpuapi/vpuapi.c b/interdrv/cvi_vc_drv/vcodec/vpuapi/vpuapi.c
index f577425..41f040e 100644
--- a/interdrv/cvi_vc_drv/vcodec/vpuapi/vpuapi.c
+++ b/interdrv/cvi_vc_drv/vcodec/vpuapi/vpuapi.c
@@ -14,6 +14,7 @@
 //
 //--=========================================================================--
 
+#include <linux/delay.h>
 #include "vpuapifunc.h"
 #include "product.h"
 #include "main_helper.h"
@@ -3604,7 +3605,7 @@ RetCode cviVPU_LockAndCheck(EncHandle handle, int targetState, int timeout_ms)
 			if (pCodecInst->state != targetState) {
 				CVI_VC_TRACE("state = %d\n", pCodecInst->state);
 				LeaveVcodecLock(pCodecInst->coreIdx);
-				cond_resched();
+				usleep_range(200, 400);
 			} else {
 				break;
 			}
